Runtime tests for the module built against unpatched nginx.

Build nginx with the module and install it into <build>/inst, e.g.

    ./configure --prefix=<build>/inst --add-dynamic-module=/path/to/module
    make && make install

then run, for each load balancing method and with/without "zone":

    python3 run_test.py <build> rr|hash|chash|ip_hash|least_conn|random|random2 0|1

run_test.py starts Python backends (backend.py): A is healthy, B serves
traffic but fails /health, C is not running, D is healthy but marked
"down" in the configuration. It checks the status page, that no request
reaches B, C or D while they are down, that B and C get traffic again
once they recover, backup servers, reload, and that checks keep running
with check_keepalive_requests > 1. PORT_BASE (default 18080) moves the
ports so several builds can be tested at once.

resolve_test.py <build> (nginx 1.27.3+) uses a small DNS responder
(dns.py). A "resolve" server whose address is not in the configuration
must be checked as a dynamic peer: down while its backend is dead, up once
it comes back, kept over a reload, and its check slot released once the
name stops resolving. Another "resolve" server keeps being removed and
re-added by the resolver, and must be marked down again each time.

upsync_test.py <build> needs nginx built with nginx-upsync-module as well
(https://github.com/weibocom/nginx-upsync-module). It serves the servers
from a fake consul (consul.py) and checks that servers added by upsync are
checked, that dead ones get no traffic, that they recover, that removed
ones have their check slots released, and that state is kept over a
reload.

nginx built --with-stream also gets the stream tests, which proxy raw TCP
to the same backends:

    python3 stream_test.py <build> rr|hash|chash|least_conn|random|random2 0|1

checks a stream upstream with an http check, one with a tcp check and one
with a backup server, next to an http upstream of the same name: no
connection reaches B, C or D while they are down, B and C get connections
again once they recover, the status page lists the stream servers with
"upstream_type": "stream", state is kept over a reload, and checks keep
running with check_keepalive_requests > 1. stream_resolve_test.py (nginx
1.27.3+) is resolve_test.py for a stream upstream, with the http block
first, and stream_upsync_test.py is upsync_test.py for a stream upstream
with nginx-stream-upsync-module
(https://github.com/xiaokai-wang/nginx-stream-upsync-module).

common.py holds the helpers shared by the tests other than run_test.py.
